WEBVTT

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:07.160
Yuma.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:08.940
Hey, Yuma!

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:12.260
Kattobing...

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:12.990
Sheesh!

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.140
Ouch!

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.140
What are you doing?

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:19.950
Class ended.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:22.310
Oh.

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:23.460
Sheesh...

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:26.910
All right! It’s kattobing time!

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:31.420
The teacher said to read
the letter he sent to everyone’s homes.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:33.950
What letter?

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:35.050
Sheesh...

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:38.100
Our school has open house this Saturday.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:43.400
Kotori, which of your parents
are coming to open house?

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.670
Sorry, Yuma.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:49.030
Don’t worry about it!

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:51.280
I’m fine!

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:56.910
This Saturday...

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:59.780
Open house is annoying.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:03.080
Yuma, what’s open house?

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:08.590
Our parents come to our school and observe our class to make sure that we’re studying.

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:10.750
But your parents are...

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:14.260
It can be anyone in the family.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:17.470
I have my sister and my grandma.

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:21.430
I’m home.

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:23.550
Huh?

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:26.840
Grandma, I’m coming in.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:28.650
Welcome home.

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.280
Umm-

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:32.410
Do you like this kimono?

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:38.360
I’m going to wear this for my class reunion on Saturday.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:40.030
Saturday?

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:42.620
I wonder how Tome and Okiku are doing.

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:46.750
I wonder what my first love Kokichi is up to.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.700
Sis!

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:52.230
I won’t let you borrow your allowance in advance.

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:53.500
That’s not what I want to talk about!

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:57.880
Then what? I’m busy with this news report.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:01.010
Hey, Tetsuko.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:05.180
I forgot that the class reunion was this Saturday!

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:07.640
Of course I’m going!

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:10.830
I’m looking forward to seeing everyone.

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:13.530
Yuma?

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:42.720
Good morning, Kotori!

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:43.750
Good morning!

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:44.680
Good morning!

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:47.590
Which of your parents is coming to open house?

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:48.940
My mom.

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:52.690
My papa was excited,
so I think they’re both coming.

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:54.270
Same here.

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:58.860
We have the vaulting boxes
for P.E. today, right?

00:02:58.860 --> 00:02:59.860
Yeah.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:03.770
That means we can see Tsukumo’s kattobing.

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:06.180
My papa wanted to see that!

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:10.790
Oh no! I’m late!

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.410
Ouch!

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:16.460
What are you doing?

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.250
Sis!

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:21.760
Why are you staring?

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:26.680
Everyone looks good in the right clothes.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:29.060
You look lovely, Grandma.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:33.430
Really? It’s because I still feel like a young girl.

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:35.030
Yuma?

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:37.500
There’s school on a Saturday?

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:38.970
I guess.

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:42.040
Don’t tell me it’s for remedial classes!

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:44.040
It’s not! I’m going!

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:44.620
Hey!

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.540
Hurry up!

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:54.690
Yuma, why didn’t you tell them
about open house?

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:56.880
Because it would be bad.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:01.270
My sister and grandma
were both looking forward for today.

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:03.050
I see.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:06.510
Yeah! And I’m no longer a kid anymore.

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:09.440
They don’t need to come to all my open houses.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:12.940
All right! I’ll still make it in time!

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.750
Kattobing...

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:18.810
It’s missing!

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:19.780
What is it?

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:21.880
My King’s Key is missing!

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:23.630
What?

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:30.750
Whether it’s rain, wind, blizzard or the scorching sun

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:33.870
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:36.670
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:41.050
Freedom begins by accepting differences Dance and create the universe

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:48.450
In truth, I was sad until I met you

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:54.930
I lied, thinking it was easier to be alone

00:04:54.930 --> 00:05:01.530
Even though we don’t like the same books or hobbies

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:05.400
You’re the only one who agreed with me

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:08.530
Joy and sadness and anger and do re mi fa so la ti do

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:10.340
There’s no harmony and scenario without differences

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.700
Everyone is not the same

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:18.630
That’s the reason for living

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:23.880
Even if the sounds are dissonant at times

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:29.300
That’s why I never give up
I believe my strength will get me through

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:32.560
I travel to the edge of the world

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:37.020
The sights I see with you are the truth

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:39.860
Whether it’s rain, wind, blizzard or the scorching sun

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:43.110
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:46.490
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:50.160
Freedom begins by accepting differences Dance and create the universe

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:59.040
Yuma, did you really drop it?

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:05.420
\hThe Kattobing Promise\h

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:05.420
Number 19:

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.960
If you did, you must find it.

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:05.420
It’s very important to me.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.970
Be quiet! I know!

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:13.110
It’s important to me too,
because my dad gave it to me!

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:15.270
Your dad?

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:21.610
This was inside Yuma’s father’s King’s Key.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:27.450
Is there a connection between me and his father?

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:28.200
Yuma.

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:32.290
What kind of person was your father?

00:06:32.290 --> 00:06:34.170
My dad?

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:38.930
He was different.

00:06:38.930 --> 00:06:41.630
He really hated the word “boring.”

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:46.840
My dad taught me about kattobing.

00:06:55.990 --> 00:06:57.390
What’s wrong, Yuma?

00:06:57.820 --> 00:06:59.850
Climb, Yuma!

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:03.060
It’s impossible! I can’t climb this!

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:05.820
Yuma, kattobing!

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:11.990
It’s unfair!

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:15.490
Dad only went with Yuma again!

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:20.240
He said that they were going to talk man-to-man.

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:21.290
What’s with that?

00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:23.850
How lame!

00:07:25.690 --> 00:07:28.550
I wish I was a boy.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:37.690
Let’s forget about those selfish boys while the girls have a delicious meal.

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:39.640
Really, Mom?

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:44.000
Hooray! I love you, Mom!

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:47.300
I want Italian!

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:50.110
Akari, you’re barefoot!

00:07:56.380 --> 00:07:58.250
The sun is setting.

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:01.830
What is it?

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:04.830
Did something happen at school?

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:12.300
You idiot!

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:15.800
You have no skills to be a champion!

00:08:16.270 --> 00:08:19.030
Be quiet! I’m going to become duel champion!

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:21.480
I’m saying you can’t!

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:26.480
I promise to become champion!

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:29.350
It’s nothing.

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:32.450
I see.

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:35.410
However...

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:36.580
However?

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:39.870
I don’t want to go to school anymore.

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:41.050
Why not?

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:43.830
Because school is boring.

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:48.300
Yuma, do you know about multiple other worlds?

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:50.490
What’s that?

00:08:50.490 --> 00:08:55.800
It looks like there’s only one world, but we’re actually connected to many other worlds.

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:02.510
This world has two worlds.

00:09:02.510 --> 00:09:09.480
One is a world full of hope, and the other is a boring world with no hope.

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:12.940
These two worlds are connected.

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:15.090
Really?

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:15.950
Yeah.

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:21.870
The world of hope is full of adventure and romance, and it’s waiting for you to challenge it.

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:26.660
But you’re in the boring world right now.

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:31.840
As long as you’re in the boring world, you can only think negatively.

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:35.970
Then how can I go to the other world?

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:38.410
That’s simple!

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:42.780
You have to set a goal that you want to achieve.

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:44.180
What kind of goal?

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:46.690
It can be anything!

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:51.990
Like doing one good deed a day or becoming the champion of speed eating and speed pooing!

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:53.670
Speed pooing?

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:58.410
Yuma, what’s your goal?

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:01.500
My goal?

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:06.200
My goal is to become the duel champion of the world.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:08.410
You have a spectacular goal!

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:11.440
But when I say that, everyone makes fun of me.

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:13.170
Don’t worry about that.

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:14.440
But I do.

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:19.660
You care about what others think because you’re not seriously trying to achieve your goal.

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:25.920
If you work hard towards your goal, you won’t have time to care about what they think.

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:28.500
Keep challenging!

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:32.610
Stop thinking that the world is boring.

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:37.070
You can go to the world of hope.

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:39.900
Yuma, always keep challenging.

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:43.030
That will lift your spirits.

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:45.580
All right! Let’s duel!

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:47.240
Dad will teach you!

00:10:47.240 --> 00:10:48.480
Here?

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:49.410
Yeah!

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:52.000
It’ll feel great! And tomorrow...

00:10:52.580 --> 00:10:55.330
We’ll go even higher and duel!

00:10:57.760 --> 00:10:59.520
Duel champion...

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:00.590
Yeah.

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:04.810
Dad truly believed that I could become one.

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:09.310
So if I give up, that means I’m betraying my dad.

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:25.280
Here I go, Yuma.

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:30.250
I overlay Level 4 Gogogo Golem
and Ganbara Knight!

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:33.960
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:37.460
Xyz Summon!

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:41.210
But I don’t have any Xyz Monsters in my deck.

00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:44.010
Dad!

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:48.170
Dad...

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:49.340
What is it?

00:11:49.340 --> 00:11:50.980
Dad, what’s your goal?

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:58.030
Mine? My goal is to go
to the edge of the world.

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:02.890
What’s so funny?

00:12:02.890 --> 00:12:05.160
Because you said the edge of the world.

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:07.090
Dad, you’re silly.

00:12:07.090 --> 00:12:08.830
The world is round.

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:11.160
There’s no such thing!

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:13.790
I guess that’s true.

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:15.780
Sheesh, Dad!

00:12:18.580 --> 00:12:23.260
But I might be the one who was wrong.

00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:25.550
What do you mean?

00:12:26.190 --> 00:12:32.060
Dad once told me a story about the edge of the world.

00:12:55.150 --> 00:12:56.500
What was that?

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:58.390
What’s this?

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:11.770
Dear!

00:13:17.170 --> 00:13:18.860
Dear!

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:32.020
Mirai!

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:36.870
Kazuma, don’t do it!

00:13:37.390 --> 00:13:40.840
I’m not giving up hope! There’s still hope!

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:43.450
I have hope that you’ll live!

00:13:43.450 --> 00:13:46.050
I promise to return.

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:54.810
Kazuma!

00:13:55.180 --> 00:13:59.810
That’s when Dad may have seen something.

00:14:02.180 --> 00:14:03.880
Where am I?

00:14:04.750 --> 00:14:06.860
It can’t be...

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:10.060
Is this the edge of the world?

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:41.580
They miraculously rescued my dad
a week after the accident.

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:42.580
Dad!

00:14:42.580 --> 00:14:43.960
Dad!

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:47.860
I’m fine. There’s nothing to worry about.

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:52.770
Dad, thank goodness!

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:57.700
He probably saw something.

00:14:57.700 --> 00:14:59.460
What did he see?

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:01.130
The edge of the world.

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:03.280
The edge of the world?

00:15:03.280 --> 00:15:07.700
My dad said that this world has various worlds.

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:13.350
He probably saw something that connects this world with another world.

00:15:16.920 --> 00:15:19.430
Connect this world with another world...

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:23.730
Is that the power of the King’s Key?

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:25.820
Oh yeah!

00:15:26.260 --> 00:15:28.610
I was here when...

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:34.410
I activate the spell card Soul of Fire!

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:40.670
I win.

00:15:40.670 --> 00:15:43.380
It’s impossible for you to become a champion!

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:45.910
Be quiet! I promise to become one!

00:15:45.910 --> 00:15:47.550
Then beat me.

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:49.480
If you do, I’ll believe you.

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:50.780
That’s right!

00:15:50.780 --> 00:15:53.280
But it’s impossible for you, kid.

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:55.500
Because you’re a kid.

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:59.030
I...

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:01.840
Kattobing!

00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:09.270
Dad!

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:11.240
Kattobing, Yuma!

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:13.240
Kattobing?

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:15.240
Kattobing means to challenge.

00:16:15.770 --> 00:16:19.200
It’s a heart that never gives up!

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:28.800
Take a new step, Yuma!

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:33.010
That King’s Key will give you power!

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:37.000
King’s Key...

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:45.020
That’s right! I’ll never give up!

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:48.250
I’m kattobing!

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:51.070
And that was it for Dad.

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:55.360
He said that he would keep
teaching me how to duel, but...

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:03.190
To summarize...

00:17:03.190 --> 00:17:05.470
She’s attractive!

00:17:06.870 --> 00:17:10.860
An adult woman has a certain charm
that Mizuki doesn’t have.

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:13.840
When it comes to that, Kotori is far behind.

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:19.050
Fine, Mom!

00:17:21.950 --> 00:17:23.280
DNA...

00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:24.890
...is scary.

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:27.990
Yuma isn’t here yet.

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:29.760
Yuma...

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:33.820
I’m all the way back home!

00:17:34.220 --> 00:17:36.990
But it was worth it.

00:17:38.270 --> 00:17:40.950
The King’s Key is here!

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:47.620
Dad and Mom, I’m going.

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:52.400
Long time no see.

00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:55.110
Haru, I’m glad you could come.

00:17:55.110 --> 00:17:56.610
What do you mean?

00:17:56.610 --> 00:18:01.080
If I remember correctly,
Kotori and Yuma are classmates.

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:05.020
That’s right. Kotori visits often.

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:07.720
Thank you for your kindness.

00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:10.260
Yone, you should come visit me.

00:18:10.260 --> 00:18:14.000
I recently acquired delicious green tea.

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:15.930
Well...

00:18:15.930 --> 00:18:17.960
What were we talking about?

00:18:17.960 --> 00:18:21.030
If I remember correctly, Yuma and Kotori are...

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:23.970
They’re classmates.

00:18:23.970 --> 00:18:26.870
Kotori visits often.

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:29.350
Thank you for your kindness.

00:18:30.450 --> 00:18:33.130
What were we talking about?

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:36.080
Tetsuko, long time no see!

00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:37.300
It’s been awhile!

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:40.820
Yuma always gets Tetsuo in trouble.

00:18:40.820 --> 00:18:42.680
So does Tetsuo.

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:44.260
You must be busy.

00:18:44.260 --> 00:18:45.690
Yeah.

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:47.520
That’s the hard part of being a freelance reporter.

00:18:47.990 --> 00:18:50.570
So that means Haru went to the school.

00:18:51.270 --> 00:18:54.030
Because today is open house.

00:18:54.030 --> 00:18:56.010
Tetsuo was talking about it.

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:00.970
That guy...

00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:02.110
What’s wrong?

00:19:02.110 --> 00:19:03.510
Sorry! An emergency!

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:04.370
Akari!

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:09.830
That guy...

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:12.090
He was thinking about us.

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:13.800
Dad...

00:19:15.430 --> 00:19:16.800
Akari.

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:20.930
What is it? You suddenly look serious.

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:23.760
Be careful of Yuma’s dueling.

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:28.240
His dueling will someday lead to great destiny.

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:31.240
What do you mean?

00:19:31.240 --> 00:19:32.800
You’ll know eventually.

00:19:32.800 --> 00:19:35.320
Sheesh! It’s always about Yuma!

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:38.740
It’s because you’re the older sister, Akari.

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:40.250
What’s up with that?

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:44.370
Since you’re the older sister, you’ve been able to spend more time with us.

00:19:44.980 --> 00:19:48.650
Yuma will spend less time with us than you.

00:19:48.650 --> 00:19:52.710
Someday, we won’t be with you anymore.

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:55.060
I don’t understand!

00:19:55.060 --> 00:19:57.240
I feel like I’m losing out!

00:20:07.550 --> 00:20:09.060
Yuma!

00:20:09.550 --> 00:20:10.780
Umm...

00:20:10.780 --> 00:20:12.780
Hurry up and take your seat.

00:20:12.780 --> 00:20:14.720
I’m sorry.

00:20:16.990 --> 00:20:18.750
Next up is Mizuki and the class representative!

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:19.530
Right!

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:20.950
Do your best, Takashi!

00:20:20.950 --> 00:20:22.450
Kotori, fight!

00:20:23.670 --> 00:20:26.450
To summarize, I’ll try my best!

00:20:31.010 --> 00:20:34.010
Ouch!

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:41.670
No one from Yuma’s family came.

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:43.590
Yuma...

00:20:48.090 --> 00:20:50.020
Yuma!

00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:53.310
Yuma!

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:56.020
Sister and grandma, why are you here?

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:58.690
Why didn’t you tell us?

00:20:58.690 --> 00:21:03.610
That’s right! Did you think we would have a good time if we ditched you?

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:05.910
Sister... Grandma...

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:11.540
Yuma, kattobing!

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:12.580
Go!

00:21:14.220 --> 00:21:15.540
All right!

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:19.130
I’ll try for twenty!

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:29.790
What is it, Yuma?

00:21:29.790 --> 00:21:31.720
They’re watching.

00:21:35.230 --> 00:21:37.610
Dad, Mom...

00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:45.110
I feel like I can see them too.

00:21:45.110 --> 00:21:46.540
Go, Yuma!

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:48.110
Do your best!

00:21:48.110 --> 00:21:49.910
Yuma may succeed today!

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:50.810
Yeah!

00:21:50.810 --> 00:21:52.790
Do your best, Yuma!

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:55.550
Observation #14:

00:21:55.550 --> 00:21:58.920
Yuma, everyone loves you.

00:21:58.920 --> 00:22:00.590
Go, Yuma!

00:22:00.590 --> 00:22:01.460
Yeah!

00:22:02.530 --> 00:22:06.800
I’m kattobing!

00:22:12.890 --> 00:22:15.770
Let’s start the duel!

00:22:15.770 --> 00:22:17.400
This week’s quiz:

00:22:17.400 --> 00:22:21.410
What’s the term for summoning a monster using a card effect?

00:22:21.410 --> 00:22:24.900
Normal Summon or Special Summon?

00:22:30.160 --> 00:22:35.020
Today’s test is hard
Can’t avoid pleasure and temptation

00:22:35.020 --> 00:22:40.000
I want to go home and watch TV
Recent cartoons are entertaining

00:22:49.930 --> 00:22:54.610
Anyway, tests are hard
Language, math and English are especially hard

00:22:54.610 --> 00:22:59.600
Average scores in science and social studies
I’m only good at P.E.

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:02.020
(Wait, Baby!) The expected

00:23:02.480 --> 00:23:04.920
(What’s that, Baby!) Answers

00:23:04.920 --> 00:23:07.030
(Wait a sec, Baby!) Remember them

00:23:07.490 --> 00:23:08.950
(What are we!? Baby!) For who

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:13.760
Let’s say I wrote the correct answers on that sheet

00:23:13.760 --> 00:23:18.160
Will that change the future a year or a decade from now?

00:23:18.610 --> 00:23:23.700
The world I drew at the edge of dreams

00:23:23.700 --> 00:23:28.210
Someday I’ll race in the sky

00:23:28.210 --> 00:23:33.350
Nobody can threaten my heart

00:23:33.350 --> 00:23:37.290
Nothing is correct!

00:23:40.800 --> 00:23:42.730
Number 96!

00:23:42.730 --> 00:23:48.650
It used its shadow powers
to possess Astral and control my body!

00:23:48.650 --> 00:23:50.900
Now you’re my minion!

00:23:51.910 --> 00:23:52.660
Yuma!

00:23:52.660 --> 00:23:55.950
I’ve become the strongest Number!

00:23:55.950 --> 00:23:57.450
Run away, Tetsuo...

00:23:57.450 --> 00:24:01.460
Never! I promise to win the duel and rescue you!

00:24:01.460 --> 00:24:10.010
\h\hThe Dark Number: Dark Yuma vs Tetsuo\h\h

00:24:01.460 --> 00:24:06.670
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“The Dark Number: Dark Yuma vs Tetsuo”

00:24:07.150 --> 00:24:10.010
I’m kattobing!

00:24:11.830 --> 00:24:13.740
The answer is...

00:24:13.740 --> 00:24:15.830
Special Summon!

00:24:15.830 --> 00:24:25.040
Using monster, spell or trap card effects to summon a monster is called a Special Summon!
